.TH QUADRF-DNS-UPDATE 8 "August 2026" "QuadRF" "QuadRF"
.SH NAME
quadrf-dns-update \- publish the QuadRF names on the station interface
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B quadrf-dns-update
.SH DESCRIPTION
When wlan0 holds a global address, writes a dnsmasq snippet that resolves
.BR QUADRF_TLS_DOMAIN ,
.B quadrf.local
and
.B quadrf
to whatever address wlan0 currently has, then reloads dnsmasq. When wlan0 has
no address the snippet is removed instead.
.PP
.I /etc/network/if-up.d/quadrf-dns
calls this whenever wlan0 comes up, and
.B quadrf apply
calls it once at install time. The file is only rewritten when its contents
change, so repeated calls do not disturb running clients.
.PP
The reload is deliberately detached from the caller: at boot
.B network.target
waits on ifup@wlan0 while dnsmasq waits on
.BR network-online.target ,
and a synchronous restart here stalls both for about forty-five seconds.
.SH FILES
.TP
.I /etc/dnsmasq.d/quadrf-wlan0-lan.conf
The generated snippet.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR quadrf (1),
.BR quadrf.conf (5),
.BR quadrf-hotspot (8)
